{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 2: The OR Gate",
  "description": "Same architecture as AND - different weights!\n\nChallenge: Adjust the weights to make this output ON when \nEITHER input (or both) is high.\n\nKey insight: The neuron's \"personality\" (AND vs OR) comes from \nits weights and bias, not its structure.\n\nHint: OR gate needs a bias around -0.5 (lower threshold than AND).\nWith inputs 0 or 1, when should the weighted sum exceed 0.5?",
