    {
      "id": "comment-e747de7d-2099-438a-8a75-dda900ff1364",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "name": "Welcome",
      "position": [
        50,
        50
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "# OR Gate - One is Enough!\n\nThe OR gate outputs ON when **either** input is high (or both).\n\n## To Do and Notice\n\n1. **Try all combinations**: (0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1)\n2. **Look at the weights**: How do they differ from AND?\n3. **The bias trick**: A bias of -0.5 means you only need ONE input to pass the threshold\n\n## The Math\n\n```\nresult = (A * 1.0) + (B * 1.0) + (-0.5)\n```\n\nWith bias = -0.5:\n- (0,0): 0 + 0 - 0.5 = -0.5 (OFF)\n- (1,0): 1 + 0 - 0.5 = +0.5 (ON!)\n- (0,1): 0 + 1 - 0.5 = +0.5 (ON!)\n- (1,1): 1 + 1 - 0.5 = +1.5 (ON!)\n\n**Challenge**: Can you make an OR gate with a different bias?",
        "width": 450,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Tutorial introduction"
    }
  ],
